entries.definition_en:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.24; 
 son of: Elioenai (H0454B); 
 brother of: Eliashib (H0475), Pelaiah (H6411B), Akkub (H6126), Johanan (H3110I), Delaiah (H1806) and Anani (H6054)
Another name of ho.dav.yah (הוֹדַוְיָה "Hodaviah" H1938G) 
 § Hodaiah = "praise ye Jehovah"
 son of the royal line of Judah

Someone descended from Heber who was a man of the tribe of Asher living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.17; 
 son of: Beriah (H1283); 
 brother of: Malchiel (H4439); 
 father of: Japhlet (H3310), Shomer (H7763H), Hotham (H2369) and Shua (H7774)
Group of che.ver (חֶ֫בֶר "Heber" H2268) 
 § Heberites , of Heber
 descendants of Heber

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.23.35; also called in KJV: Hezrai; 
 § Hezro or Hezrai = "enclosed"
 the Carmelite, one of David's 30 mighty warriors in his guard

A man living at the time before the Flood, first mentioned at Gen.5.12; 
 son of: Kenan (H7018); 
 father of: Jared (H3382); also called Mahalaleel (NIV: Mahalel) at Luk.3.37; 
Also named: Maleleēl (Μαλελεήλ "Mahalaleel" G3121)
 § Mahalaleel = "praise of God"
1) son of Cainan and the 4th in descent from Adam in the line of Seth
2) a descendant of Perez, the son of Judah

A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.26.7; 
 son of: Shemaiah (H8098I); 
 brother of: Othni (H6273), Rephael (H7501), Obed (H5744J), Elihu (H0453I) and Semachiah (H5565)
 § Elzabad = "God has given"
1) a Gadite warrior who aided David
2) a Korhite Levite

A man of the tribe of Gad living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.16; 
 son of: Gad (H1410); 
 brother of: Ziphion (H6837), Haggi (H2291), Ezbon (H0675), Eri (H6179), Arod (H0720) and Areli (H0692)
Also named: shu.ni (שׁוּנִי "Shunite" H7765) 
 § Shuni = "fortunate"
 son of Gad and progenitor of the family of Shunites
